
MAINTENANCE HISTORY
-------------------

The administrator frequently used command-line utilities
to preserve sensitive information.

A previous maintenance note contained the following:

"Not everything that looks unreadable is encrypted."

Another note mentioned that the administrator preferred
representations that could survive being copied between systems.

The original files were rarely left untouched.

A final maintenance reminder:

"Always identify the file format before attempting
to recover its original contents."

END OF HISTORY

